@page "/visualmcp/tools"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Capabilities — VisualMCP";
    ViewData["Description"] = "What is in the box of VisualMCP: navigation and understanding, analysis, semantic refactoring, the code-style engine, Razor/Blazor/XAML layers, runtime work, the wider loop around the code, and the metacode model.";
    ViewData["DocsKey"] = "tools";
    ViewData["DocsGitHub"] = "https://github.com/matteofabbri/VisualMCP/blob/master/docs/tools.md";
}

<partial name="_VisualMcpDocsNav" />

<header class="page-head docs-head">
    <div>
        <h1>Capabilities</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            More than 400 tools, one idea behind all of them: the answer comes
            from the compiler's view of the solution, not from text. These are
            the families, and the questions each one answers.
        </p>
    </div>
</header>

<div class="docs-body prose">
    <h2>Navigation and understanding</h2>
    <p>
        Symbols, references, callers, implementations, inheritance, type
        outlines, declaration source and project docs. The lookup that greps
        try to approximate — resolved through Roslyn, so overloads, generics,
        partial types and interface dispatch are answered exactly.
        <code>find_symbol</code>, <code>read_symbol</code>,
        <code>find_references</code>, <code>find_callers</code>,
        <code>find_implementations</code>, <code>get_type_members</code>,
        <code>get_symbol_info</code>, <code>get_xml_docs</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Analysis</h2>
    <p>
        Whole-solution audit, compiler diagnostics <strong>and the mechanical
        ones fixed</strong>, inspections with code fixes, cyclomatic and
        cognitive complexity with the lines that own the score, static Big-O
        estimates, churn × complexity hotspots, dead code, structural
        duplicates, CWE-tagged security findings, async anti-patterns,
        allocation anti-patterns, dependency injection and namespace coupling.
        <code>solution_audit</code>, <code>inspect_code</code>,
        <code>complexity_report</code>, <code>analyze_complexity</code>,
        <code>find_security_issues</code>, <code>find_dead_code</code>,
        <code>fix_complexity</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Refactoring</h2>
    <p>
        A full semantic refactoring catalogue — rename, extract method, extract
        class and superclass, change signature, move type and members, convert
        between kinds — most of it compiler-gated: an edit that would introduce
        an error is refused, and every write is recorded so it can be reverted.
        <code>apply_rename</code>, <code>extract_method</code>,
        <code>change_signature</code>, <code>safe_delete</code>,
        <code>move_type</code>, <code>reduce_complexity</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Code style</h2>
    <p>
        <code>simplify_code</code> applies the IDE's mechanical quick fixes
        without an IDE: the rewrite engine behind the quick-fix popup, with a
        per-document compiler gate, option-driven rules that respect your
        <code>.editorconfig</code>, and a recorded, revertible edit history.
        Visual Basic has its own layer, <code>simplify_vb_code</code>.
        <code>apply_code_fix</code> executes the analyzers' own fixers;
        <code>code_cleanup</code>, <code>format_code</code> and
        <code>optimize_usings</code> complete the sweep.
    </p>

    <h2>Razor, Blazor and XAML</h2>
    <p>
        Razor pages and Blazor components are read from disk with a dedicated
        scanner: inventory and wiring, markup/accessibility/maintainability
        rules, and CWE-tagged security rules — with verified, history-recorded
        edits. XAML has its own layer: inventory with the project's dialect,
        markup diagnostics, <strong>binding paths checked against their data
        type</strong>, the element tree and navigation by name, key and style.
        <code>razor_pages</code>, <code>analyze_razor_pages</code>,
        <code>find_razor_vulnerabilities</code>, <code>razor_edit</code>,
        <code>xaml_pages</code>, <code>xaml_bindings</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Runtime work</h2>
    <p>
        Build with structured diagnostics, run, test with coverage, debug
        through a real DAP debugger with breakpoints and watch windows, run
        benchmarks, and profile a live .NET process — CPU, GC, allocations,
        I/O, locks, dumps — with verdicts in plain language.
        <code>build_project</code>, <code>run_tests</code>,
        <code>get_test_coverage_map</code>, <code>debug_launch</code>,
        <code>quick_benchmark</code>, <code>profile_slowdown</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>The wider loop</h2>
    <p>
        The plumbing around the code: NuGet package facts, vulnerability checks
        and fixes, .NET modernization with a build gate that rolls back, EF
        Core migrations, Git and GitHub, Docker, repository scaffolding
        (licenses, CONTRIBUTING, CI workflows), a solution-scoped kanban board
        with memory, and <code>run_plan</code> to execute a whole dependency
        graph of tool calls in one round trip.
        <code>update_solution</code>, <code>check_nuget_vulnerabilities</code>,
        <code>ef_migrations</code>, <code>git_conflicts</code>,
        <code>gh_pr</code>, <code>board_brief</code>, <code>run_plan</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Metacode</h2>
    <p>
        One canonical pseudocode model for C#, Visual Basic, Razor, JavaScript,
        Python, C++ and Rust — and for code recovered from binaries: .NET
        assemblies decompiled with ILSpy, native binaries recovered with
        Ghidra. The same algorithm prints the same body whichever frontend
        produced it, so two spellings of an algorithm can be compared line by
        line, and a decompiled library can be queried like source.
        <code>metacode_translate</code>, <code>metacode_compare</code>,
        <code>decompile_to_metacode</code>, <code>analyze_native_binary</code>.
    </p>

    <p>
        The complete catalogue — every tool, grouped by area, with a one-line
        description — is the
        <a href="https://github.com/matteofabbri/VisualMCP/blob/master/docs/tools.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tool catalogue in the repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>;
        the guides in this area show the ways of working with each family.
    </p>
</div>

